# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Abaqus run artifacts
# Produced every time the solver runs; FEMUP_tools.py already deletes most of
# them between iterations, but a cancelled run leaves them behind.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.odb
*.lck
*.msg
*.sta
*.com
*.sim
*.prt
*.dat
*.res
*.mdl
*.stt
*.abq
*.pac
*.sel
*.rec
*.rpy
*.rpy.*
*.023
*.SMABulk
*.log

# Per-iteration copies of the input deck
*_iter.inp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files regenerated by the plug-in
# Re-created from scratch every time the corresponding button is pressed, so
# there is no reason to track them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*_outer_points.txt
Launch_From_Python_run.py
Launch_Sensitivity_Analysis_run.py
log_ch_*.txt
Reference_sheet.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Calibration results
# Uncomment if you prefer not to publish the output of your own runs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#Calibration_Results.txt
#Calibrated_Parameters.txt
#Final_Cost_Function.txt
#Convergence_*.png
#MAC_Matrix_*.png
#Frequencies_Comparison.png
#Sensitivity_Report_*.txt
#Sensitivity_Plot_*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Revit / Python / Windows
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Revit writes numbered backups of a family as "<name>.0001.rfa"
*.[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].rfa
*.[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].rvt
__pycache__/
*.pyc
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*
